---
title: Day Ahead Stripped Goose
course: Main
source: Jamie Oliver
servings: 8
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: British
---

Remove the giblets etc from the @goose{5.5%kg} cavity. Rub the @./Savoury/Old English Christmas Rub{} all over the goose, both inside and out, and leave in the fridge overnight.

Place a baking tray on the bottom shelf of the oven to catch the fat, and a rack on the next shelf up. Preheat the oven to 160°C. Stuff the goose with the @fresh rosemary{4%sprigs}, @clementines{4}(halved), and @cinnamon{1%stick}. Wrap the legs in tinfoil to stop them from burning. Using a fork or the tip of a sharp knife, prick the fatty lump above the goose’s cavity to help the fat melt out.

Place the goose, breast-side up, on to the bars of the shelf in the oven. Roast for about ~{2%hours}.

Add the @carrots{3}(chunked), @red onions{3}(quartered), and @celery{a few stalks}(chunked) to the tray; this will become the base for a gravy. Cook for another ~{1%hour}, then take the goose out of the oven and transfer it to a large board. Cover loosely with foil and leave to rest while making the gravy.

Remove the tray of vegetables and fat from the oven and sieve it, keeping back the roasted vegetables for the gravy.

Put the vegetables back into the tray they cooked in and place on the hob over a medium heat. Sprinkle over @plain flour{2%tbsp} and give everything a good stir, scraping any sticky goodness from the bottom of the tray. Cook for ~{2%minutes}, then mash up all the vegetables. Add the @port or red wine{200%ml}, and about half the @water or chicken stock{1%litre}. Let everything simmer until the consistency is right, then sieve the gravy, pushing all the goodness of the vegetables through the sieve. It can be made thinner with a little extra stock later if required. Let it cool, then keep in the fridge until needed.

Start stripping the goose. It is easiest to slice the breast off with a knife, then pull the remaining meat off using a pair of forks. Transfer the meat to a deep earthenware dish or bowl, then cover the with the strained goose fat. Scatter some @freh sage leaves{small bunch} over the top for added flavour and press them down so they are just covered in the fat. Place in the fridge.

About half an hour before serving, pop the goose meat into a low oven for about ~{25%minutes}. Once it is all hot, carefully drain away any excess fat and reheat the gravy. Fry the sage leaves in a splash of olive oil, until nice and crispy, then scatter over the goose with the @pomegranate{1}(seeded).